    {
      "@id": "x:doc",
      "@type": "Container"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "This paper therefore explores the following core research question: What might it look like to integrate the seeds of a discourse-centric infrastructure into local scientific practices, and the collaborative and institutional structures of research?",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In this section of our reflections, we describe how the local transformations of scientific practice described in §5 were enabled by technical approaches for incremental formalization of lab and reading notes into discourse nodes and edges (§6.1), as well",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n2",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Information scientists have offered a compelling diagnosis of the problem of synthesis: there is a fundamental mismatch between researchers' information needs for synthesis work, and the document-centric data model of our predominant scholarly communicatio",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n3",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To meet these information needs, information scientists propose that researchers need an infrastructure based on a discourse-oriented data model for the representation of scientific knowledge.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n4",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Our guiding approach was to develop a core user experience that enabled people to write as close to prose as they normally would (and for intrinsic benefits of advancing their own synthesis work), and author a shareable discourse graph as a natural byprodu",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n5",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Our field deployment highlighted the following key aspects of this vision: Intrinsic benefits of discourse graphing for improved synthesis (§5.1), transformed primary research and research training (§5.2), and augmented collaboration (§5.3).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n6",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Sociotechnical preconditions for successful integration, including smooth(er) incremental formalization (Shipman and Marshall, 1999) of notes into discourse nodes and edges (§6.1), and local personalization of discourse graph grammars (§6.2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n7",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "From the perspective of this model, the discourse-enhanced lab notebooks are local systems that augment synthesis. The authoring of discourse graphs in an interoperable format, and evidence of their use in collaborative research work, are seeds of distribu",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n8",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "70% of respondents who self-identified as current active users of the extension reported that the Discourse Context feature was a core part of their workflow, and 17% reporting that it was used at least on occasion. This was by far the most used extension",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n9",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Of the four users who shared a csv export of their discourse graph with us in the usage survey, we saw that these users created an average of 1.4k nodes, within the first year of usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n10",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In one of his main writing projects, he was struggling to conceptualize the contribution of his work against the existing literature, and the extension enabled him to write out and trace the 'logic line' that articulated the contribution of his work, enabl",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n11",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "He realized that he could adapt the ontological distinction between claims and evidence to his day-to-day work of forming and testing hypotheses against experimental results. This enabled him to retain rich discourse context for his inquiry, tracing his or",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n12",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "I did a 3-hour synthesis session with…(a PhD student) yesterday. I had him convert his results into result nodes (which he had been resisting) and we used a query to drop those nodes + related discourse nodes onto a canvas, to compose into what ended up be",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n13",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Instead, users relied on the built in low-friction means of relating nodes, such as simply indenting one node under another, and relying on context or (often unwritten) convention to interpret the relations.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n14",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "40% of users self-reported the grammar editor as core to their workflow, with an additional 40% reporting at least occasional usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n15",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We observed implementations of Discourse Graphs in Obsidian (see Figure 24B), Tinderbox (a longstanding visual hypertext notebook; see Figure 24C), Tana... Notably, users from the Logseq community organized an $8,000 bounty (funded in part by a grant from",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n16",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Unfortunately, the overlay was very performance-intensive, and we were unable to find workable solutions for optimizing it, given the limitations of the querying mechanisms we had technical access to for the extension, which led to very noticeable and disr",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n17",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We explored our research questions using a Research through Design (RtD) methodology... These phases of work spanned approximately 3 years, and involving direct interactions with 48 participants.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n18",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We distributed a usage survey in the Fall of 2022 to get a quantitative picture of usage... We received N=41 total responses to the survey.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The first author conducted semi-structured interviews, each lasting approximately 60–90 minutes, with N=5 users who indicated an interest in a follow-up from the usage survey.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n20",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "After initial analysis was completed in March 2024, the first author conducted member checks with N=7 key informants via email and calls.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n21",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We were able to obtain user-provided exports of data from N=4 users (5, including the author's lab) from the usage survey approximately 12 months into the deployment (in Fall of 2022).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n22",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We followed Zimmerman and Forlizzi's (Zimmerman and Forlizzi, 2014) suggested 5-step cycle for Research through Design work: 1) select a design problem or opportunity, 2) conduct design work to develop an initial framing and prototypes, 3) evaluate the des",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n23",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We therefore drew on participatory methodology (Vaughn and Jacquez, 2020) — including reflexive, detailed field notes, regular research discussions with key community members, and co-authorship of the final manuscript — to ensure that community participati",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n24",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Analysis was primarily conducted by the first author, using a general constructivist and interpretivist (Schwandt, 1994) approach. Analysis was interleaved with data collection throughout, including in reflective memos, and, once critical mass of data accu",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n25",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The user experience of this would be very similar to annotating: she would simply select the text she wants to 'mark as' evidence, press a hotkey to initiate the node authoring action, then select the appropriate node type, either with her mouse or with th",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n26",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We prototyped a Discourse Grammar Parser to enable the system to parse formal discourse relation 'edges' (e.g., support, oppose, inform) from user-defined conventions of prose writing and outlining.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n27",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Separately, inspired by previous work on visuospatial sensemaking and visual hypertext systems (e.g., IBIS (Conklin, 1987)), we also prototyped a Playground infinite canvas component where users could insert or create discourse nodes, visually cluster them",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n28",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We prototyped a Discourse Context component that provided additional associative trail navigation between notes based on discourse relations like inform/support/oppose (see Figure 8A).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n29",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We also prototyped a Synthesis Query component to enable users to perform specialized querying based on discourse graph elements and relations (e.g., find all evidence that informs my question, but opposes some claim; find all evidence that informs a quest",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n30",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We prototyped a Discourse Overlay feature that enabled users to see an in-line preview of the discourse context of a discourse node — in the form of a count of the number of discourse relations for a discourse node, as well as the number of references to t",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n31",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Users could add new discourse nodes (A), add new discourse relation patterns (B), and use a graphical layout to specify the underlying Datalog query in the Roam database that mapped to writing patterns that would enable the discourse graph extension to rec",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n32",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Abstract. Sharing, reusing, and synthesizing knowledge is central to the research process, both individually, and with others.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n33",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We explored our research questions using a Research through Design (RtD) methodology (Zimmerman and Forlizzi, 2014).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n34",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Shipman and colleagues (Shipman and Marshall, 1999) proposed the concept of incremental formalization as a means of mitigating these risks of formalisms.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n35",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The first design pattern of integrated crowdsourcing has been proposed and validated as a means of sustaining work that is beneficial for a community... (Siangliulue et al., 2016).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n36",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Edwards et al elaborate on this intuition by drawing three key implications from historical models of infrastructural development from history and sociology (Hughes, 1983).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n37",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We wonder whether users might be able to more smoothly recognize latent discourse edges in their existing work with systems that integrate AI approaches for transforming unstructured (text) data into more structured formats.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n38",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Here, again, we think there may be interesting research directions around mixed-initiative interfaces that integrate advances in argument mining (Schneider et al., 2013), claim generation (Wright et al., 2022), or scientific document information extraction",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n39",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "For example, what would happen if we enabled peer-to-peer exchange of local discourse graphs across, say, evidence synthesis groups like Cochrane, biomedical research labs, and biotech innovation companies and investing firms?",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n40",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Given the expressed and observed desire for smoother and less effortful specification of relations described in the previous section (§6.1), as well as some user data on the continued desire for easier ways to express these patterns to the extension's pars",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "This paper therefore explores the following core research question: What might it look like to integrate the seeds of a discourse-centric infrastructure into local scientific practices, and the collaborative and institutional structures of research?",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To meet these information needs, information scientists propose that researchers need an infrastructure based on a discourse-oriented data model for the representation of scientific knowledge.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r2",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Our guiding approach was to develop a core user experience that enabled people to write as close to prose as they normally would (and for intrinsic benefits of advancing their own synthesis work), and author a shareable discourse graph as a natural byprodu",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r3",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Our field deployment highlighted the following key aspects of this vision: Intrinsic benefits of discourse graphing for improved synthesis (§5.1), transformed primary research and research training (§5.2), and augmented collaboration (§5.3).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r4",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Sociotechnical preconditions for successful integration, including smooth(er) incremental formalization (Shipman and Marshall, 1999) of notes into discourse nodes and edges (§6.1), and local personalization of discourse graph grammars (§6.2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r5",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "From the perspective of this model, the discourse-enhanced lab notebooks are local systems that augment synthesis. The authoring of discourse graphs in an interoperable format, and evidence of their use in collaborative research work, are seeds of distribu",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r6",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "70% of respondents who self-identified as current active users of the extension reported that the Discourse Context feature was a core part of their workflow",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r7",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Of the four users who shared a csv export of their discourse graph with us in the usage survey, we saw that these users created an average of 1.4k nodes, within the first year of usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r8",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In one of his main writing projects, he was struggling to conceptualize the contribution of his work against the existing literature, and the extension enabled him to write out and trace the 'logic line' that articulated the contribution of his work, enabl",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r9",
