      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Instead, users relied on the built in low-friction means of relating nodes, such as simply indenting one node under another, and relying on context or (often unwritten) convention to interpret the relations.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r12",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "40% of users self-reported the grammar editor as core to their workflow, with an additional 40% reporting at least occasional usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r13",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We observed implementations of Discourse Graphs in Obsidian (see Figure 24B), Tinderbox (a longstanding visual hypertext notebook; see Figure 24C), Tana... Notably, users from the Logseq community organized an $8,000 bounty... for a full port of the Discou",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r14",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Unfortunately, the overlay was very performance-intensive, and we were unable to find workable solutions for optimizing it... which led to very noticeable and disruptive slowdowns in the user interface.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r15",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We explored our research questions using a Research through Design (RtD) methodology... These phases of work spanned approximately 3 years, and involving direct interactions with 48 participants.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r16",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We distributed a usage survey in the Fall of 2022 to get a quantitative picture of usage... We received N=41 total responses to the survey.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r17",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The first author conducted semi-structured interviews, each lasting approximately 60–90 minutes, with N=5 users who indicated an interest in a follow-up from the usage survey.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r18",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "After initial analysis was completed in March 2024, the first author conducted member checks with N=7 key informants via email and calls.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We were able to obtain user-provided exports of data from N=4 users (5, including the author's lab) from the usage survey approximately 12 months into the deployment (in Fall of 2022).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r20",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In one of his main writing projects, he was struggling to conceptualize the contribution of his work against the existing literature, and the extension enabled him to write out and trace the 'logic line' that articulated the contribution of his work, enabl",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r21",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "He realized that he could adapt the ontological distinction between claims and evidence to his day-to-day work of forming and testing hypotheses against experimental results.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r22",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "I did a 3-hour synthesis session with…(a PhD student) yesterday. I had him convert his results into result nodes (which he had been resisting) and we used a query to drop those nodes + related discourse nodes onto a canvas, to compose into what ended up be",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r23",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Instead, users relied on the built in low-friction means of relating nodes, such as simply indenting one node under another, and relying on context or (often unwritten) convention to interpret the relations.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r24",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "40% of users self-reported the grammar editor as core to their workflow, with an additional 40% reporting at least occasional usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r25",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We observed implementations of Discourse Graphs in Obsidian (see Figure 24B), Tinderbox (a longstanding visual hypertext notebook; see Figure 24C), Tana... Notably, users from the Logseq community organized an $8,000 bounty... for a full port of the Discou",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r26",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Unfortunately, the overlay was very performance-intensive, and we were unable to find workable solutions for optimizing it... which led to very noticeable and disruptive slowdowns in the user interface.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r27",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "70% of respondents who self-identified as current active users of the extension reported that the Discourse Context feature was a core part of their workflow, and 17% reporting that it was used at least on occasion.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r28",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Of the four users who shared a csv export of their discourse graph with us in the usage survey, we saw that these users created an average of 1.4k nodes, within the first year of usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r29",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "40% of users self-reported the grammar editor as core to their workflow, with an additional 40% reporting at least occasional usage.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r30",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We followed Zimmerman and Forlizzi's (Zimmerman and Forlizzi, 2014) suggested 5-step cycle for Research through Design work: 1) select a design problem or opportunity, 2) conduct design work to develop an initial framing and prototypes, 3) evaluate the des",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r31",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We therefore drew on participatory methodology (Vaughn and Jacquez, 2020) — including reflexive, detailed field notes, regular research discussions with key community members, and co-authorship of the final manuscript — to ensure that community participati",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r32",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Analysis was primarily conducted by the first author, using a general constructivist and interpretivist (Schwandt, 1994) approach. Analysis was interleaved with data collection throughout, including in reflective memos, and, once critical mass of data accu",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r33",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The user experience of this would be very similar to annotating: she would simply select the text she wants to 'mark as' evidence, press a hotkey to initiate the node authoring action, then select the appropriate node type, either with her mouse or with th",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r34",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We prototyped a Discourse Grammar Parser to enable the system to parse formal discourse relation 'edges' (e.g., support, oppose, inform) from user-defined conventions of prose writing and outlining.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r35",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Separately, inspired by previous work on visuospatial sensemaking and visual hypertext systems (e.g., IBIS (Conklin, 1987)), we also prototyped a Playground infinite canvas component where users could insert or create discourse nodes, visually cluster them",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r36",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We prototyped a Discourse Context component that provided additional associative trail navigation between notes based on discourse relations like inform/support/oppose (see Figure 8A).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r37",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We also prototyped a Synthesis Query component to enable users to perform specialized querying based on discourse graph elements and relations (e.g., find all evidence that informs my question, but opposes some claim; find all evidence that informs a quest",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r38",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We prototyped a Discourse Overlay feature that enabled users to see an in-line preview of the discourse context of a discourse node — in the form of a count of the number of discourse relations for a discourse node, as well as the number of references to t",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r39",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Users could add new discourse nodes (A), add new discourse relation patterns (B), and use a graphical layout to specify the underlying Datalog query in the Roam database that mapped to writing patterns that would enable the discourse graph extension to rec",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r40",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We wonder whether users might be able to more smoothly recognize latent discourse edges in their existing work with systems that integrate AI approaches for transforming unstructured (text) data into more structured formats.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r41",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Here, again, we think there may be interesting research directions around mixed-initiative interfaces that integrate advances in argument mining (Schneider et al., 2013), claim generation (Wright et al., 2022), or scientific document information extraction",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r42",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "For example, what would happen if we enabled peer-to-peer exchange of local discourse graphs across, say, evidence synthesis groups like Cochrane, biomedical research labs, and biotech innovation companies and investing firms?",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r43",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Given the expressed and observed desire for smoother and less effortful specification of relations described in the previous section (§6.1), as well as some user data on the continued desire for easier ways to express these patterns to the extension's pars",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n0",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Question",
        "Question"
      ],
      "title": "How can the seeds of a discourse-centric infrastructure be integrated into local scientific practices and collaborative structures of research?",
      "content": "How can the seeds of a discourse-centric infrastructure be integrated into local scientific practices and collaborative structures of research?\n\nCore research question driving the Research through Design work.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n1",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Question",
        "Question"
      ],
      "title": "What are the sociotechnical preconditions for a discourse-centric synthesis infrastructure?",
      "content": "What are the sociotechnical preconditions for a discourse-centric synthesis infrastructure?\n\nSecondary question addressed in Evaluation II.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n2",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "There is a fundamental mismatch between researchers' information needs for synthesis work and the document-centric data model of predominant scholarly communication infrastructure.",
      "content": "There is a fundamental mismatch between researchers' information needs for synthesis work and the document-centric data model of predominant scholarly communication infrastructure.\n\nDiagnosis from information science literature motivating the work.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n3",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Discourse graphs — modeling scientific knowledge as granular claims linked to evidence and context — can meet researchers' synthesis information needs.",
      "content": "Discourse graphs — modeling scientific knowledge as granular claims linked to evidence and context — can meet researchers' synthesis information needs.\n\nProposed solution from information science; basis for the design vision.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n4",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Integrating discourse graph authoring into everyday research workflows via incremental formalization and integrated crowdsourcing can enable a thriving installed base of local discourse graphs.",
      "content": "Integrating discourse graph authoring into everyday research workflows via incremental formalization and integrated crowdsourcing can enable a thriving installed base of local discourse graphs.\n\nDesign hypothesis embodied in the RoamResearch Discourse Graph extension.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n5",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "The RoamResearch Discourse Graph extension enables researchers to author local discourse graphs that improve synthesis work, enhance primary research and research training, and augment collaborative …",
      "content": "The RoamResearch Discourse Graph extension enables researchers to author local discourse graphs that improve synthesis work, enhance primary research and research training, and augment collaborative research.\n\nMain empirical claim from 2.5-year deployment with 48 researchers.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n6",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Smooth incremental formalization of notes into discourse nodes and edges, local personalization of discourse grammars, and cross-tool transferability are sociotechnical preconditions for growing a di…",
      "content": "Smooth incremental formalization of notes into discourse nodes and edges, local personalization of discourse grammars, and cross-tool transferability are sociotechnical preconditions for growing a discourse-centric infrastructure.\n\nSynthesized from Evaluation II findings.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n7",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "The observed local discourse-enhanced notebooks, their interoperable authoring, and organic spread across tools and domains constitute concrete steps toward a discourse-centric synthesis infrastructu…",
      "content": "The observed local discourse-enhanced notebooks, their interoperable authoring, and organic spread across tools and domains constitute concrete steps toward a discourse-centric synthesis infrastructure.\n\nMapping results to Edwards et al.'s infrastructure development model.",
      "created": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T15:29:09.642Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n7"
    },
    {
